<!--
    PROMOTioN's five-terminal meshed offshore HVDC benchmark network: complements promotion-dc.xiidm (PromotionDcNetwork.create,
    flat).

    Each AC grid a source behind the impedance of its short-circuit power, X/R 10: 30 GVA onshore, 3.8 GVA offshore, as D5.1's - the
    offshore ones its wind parks, as D5.1 models them. Each station a half-bridge MMC, averaged (CIGRE B4.57 type 4), on its rating:
    arms of 0.15 pu and 0.003 pu, D5.1's arm reactance and conduction losses; the submodules storing 40 ms, ours (D5.1 gives 160
    submodules an arm, not their capacitance). Their controls grid-following, Ieee14DcNetwork's stations': A1 on its DC voltage, B1
    on its DC voltage droop, the offshore stations on their power, as IIDM's control mode says. Those on their power, B1 and the
    offshore ones, get it back after an AC fault at 2 pu/s at most (faultRideThrough's activePowerRecoveryRate), ours, upstream's
    example 4's: D4.2 and D5.1 give none; A1, on its DC voltage, has no power to ramp.

    No DC reactor, where D5.1 has 50 to 150 mH a pole: on those controls, tuned for stations without one, A1 does not hold the DC
    voltage with one - run 2026-11-08 in PSCAD Professional, let go at 2 s, its DC voltage loop swinging and growing within 1 s at
    0.2 H a station (100 mH a pole, the two in series), within 1.5 s at 0.05 H, B1 driven to its current limit and the DC voltage
    to 1.2 to 1.7 pu; without, every station on its load flow. A braking chopper at each onshore station, A1 and B1, as D4.2's:
    1200 MW across its DC terminal, beyond its arms, conducting linearly from 1.05 to 1.1 pu. Each cable one lumped pi of the 640 kV
    conductor: 2 L and C / 2 of CIGRE B4's +-400 kV per-km pole data (2.615 mH, 0.1908 uF).

    Each cable's breakers K{cable}_{station} hybrid DC breakers, as D4.2's fully selective protection has them: a 100 mH current-
    limiting reactor a pole, 0.2 H on the one conductor, on the station's side; the energy absorber a ZnO arrester, i = 10 kA
    (v / 960 kV)^26, its protective level 1.5 pu of 640 kV at 10 kA. The reactors in series with the cables, not with the stations,
    A1 holds the DC voltage with them - run 2026-11-08 in PSCAD Professional, every station on its load flow.
-->
